2026-11-20T05:35:28.3212413Z   ok   _main: --through takes the marker and no block
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3213010Z Run one block of tests/features.py, from a marker line to the next block.
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3213379Z 
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3213839Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3214759Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... --through "<marker line>"
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3215599Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py --emit-prelude OUT "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3216038Z 
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3216379Z features.py runs every block in one process, which takes tens of minutes on a
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3217115Z loaded seat; a mutation proof needs only the block that pins the mutated line.
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3217828Z The block is the text from the line containing START up to END (default: the
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3218481Z script's closing ``sys.exit``), executed in the namespace features.py's own
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3219111Z header builds -- ``R``, ``Coord``, the harness fakes -- with ``__file__``
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3219794Z pointing at features.py, so path arithmetic inside the block resolves as in
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3220907Z the full run. Exit status is the block's ``R.close``: 0 when every check passed.
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3221527Z Run from the repository root under the CI venv.
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3221791Z 
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3222173Z ``--prelude`` (repeatable) runs one line, typically an import an earlier block
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3222944Z made, before the block. ``--through MARKER`` takes no block: it runs the whole
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3223654Z script from the top up to the line holding MARKER, the state every earlier
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3224314Z block builds, and exits with that prefix's ``R.close``.
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3224618Z 
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3224931Z ``--emit-prelude OUT`` writes to OUT the earlier top-level statements the
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3225631Z block reads, found by running it until no ``NameError`` is left: each missing
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3226356Z name takes its last binding before the use (before the block, or before the
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3226988Z prelude statement that needed it at module level). Run the block with
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3227663Z ``--prelude 'exec(open("OUT").read())'``. It derives from the tree it runs on,
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3228374Z so a mutant run needs no hand-copied prelude; exits 0 once the block runs
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3229149Z without raising (its checks are not judged), 1 on a name no earlier statement
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3229735Z binds or on any other exception.
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3230096Z 
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3230469Z ``--self-test`` runs offline: it executes a two-check block it writes itself.
2026-11-20T05:35:28.3231228Z 
